Consume only the 10-byte SOL control message, not the whole receive buffer.

When AMT reports a control-line change (e.g. the kernel's 8250 loopback probe)
and the start of a data message arrives in the same read, discarding the whole
buffer drops that header; the next read starts mid-text and amtterm aborts with
"redir_data: unknown r->buf 0x..".

Upstream status: not yet submitted.

diff --git a/redir.c b/redir.c
index 70d6100..2faed06 100644
--- a/redir.c
+++ b/redir.c
@@ -619,7 +619,7 @@ repeat:
 	    break;
 	case SOL_CONTROLS_FROM_HOST:
 	{
-	    bshift = r->blen; /* FIXME */
+	    bshift = sizeof(struct controls_from_host_message);
 	    if (r->blen < bshift)
 		goto again;
 
